Desk ticket **#4471** held **412** reports about wrong days on invites. Intake tagged almost all of them
`parser`, and the page called it one bug. The export disagrees: **two causes** share that pile.

<Callout>
Split #4471 into one engineering ticket per cause. Count each cause once.
</Callout>

## What was merged into #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What we opened

| cause | reports | what it is | desk ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| `parser` | **379** | Day-first tenants; the shared parser still reads month first, so days flip. | [GitHub issue #1](https://github.com/percy3k6/mega-dev-s01e03/issues/1) |
| `hint` | **33** | Day-first tenants on **booking-v3**; the form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` so people type month first and the tenant parser reads it their way — a different failure mode. | [GitHub issue #2](https://github.com/percy3k6/mega-dev-s01e03/issues/2) |

Five reports in the `parser` group were read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`); they stay filed
under `parser` by tenant locale, not under `hint`.

## Lessons

- Subject-line dedupe is fast; it does not know locale or form version. Re-read a big ticket with `CauseTable` before you call it one bug.
- Intake tags are guesses. The cause comes from tenant locale + channel + form (`causes.ts`).

